firewalld service for Veil, at veild.toml's defaults: the lobby ([lobby]
port), which also carries joined hosts and gateway sessions, and the web
UI ([web] listen), HTTPS over TCP and the browser client's WebTransport
over UDP. A Veil with other ports copies this to /etc/firewalld/services
and edits it there. Installing it opens nothing: add the service "veild"
to a zone.
-->
<service>
  <short>Veil</short>
  <description>Veil, the Ghost broker: its lobby for spectre logins, joined hosts and gateway sessions, and its web UI and browser client.</description>
  <port protocol="udp" port="4442"/>
  <port protocol="tcp" port="443"/>
  <port protocol="udp" port="443"/>
</service>
